            <ArticleTitle>Perforated chronic duodenal ulcer in children with coexistence of acute appendicitis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>371-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Two cases of perforation of duodenal ulcer with coexistence of acute appendicitis are reported. Current concepts regarding this unusual complication of childhood duodenal ulcer are discussed.</AbstractText>
